&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company. We free people and agents to ship what’s next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For more than a decade, Vercel has shaped how the web is built. As the team behind Next.js, v0, and AI SDK, we create products that help builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now, software is entering a new era, and the next generation of products will not just be used by people. They will be built, extended, and operated by agents.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We are building the platform for that future, trusted by companies like&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide&lt;/strong&gt;. Whether you’re building our products, supporting our customers, growing our community, or shaping our story, you’ll help define what comes next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our EBC Lead, you will build and run Vercel&#39;s Executive Briefing Center program from the ground up, turning executive visits into a signature experience that accelerates pipeline, deepens strategic relationships, and showcases where the web is going.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the full lifecycle of every briefing: qualifying requests, designing agendas tailored to each account&#39;s goals, sourcing and preparing executive and technical speakers, orchestrating flawless onsite experiences, and measuring the revenue impact of the program. You will partner daily with Sales leadership, Product, Engineering, Marketing, and our executive team, and you will be trusted to represent Vercel&#39;s brand at its most senior touchpoint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role. You will define the playbook, the space, the content library, and the metrics, then scale the program as demand grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role includes in-office anchor days on Monday, Tuesday, and Friday out of our SF office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, launch, and operate Vercel&#39;s Executive Briefing Center program, including intake, qualification criteria, and scheduling workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with account teams to define briefing objectives, build customized agendas, and align discussion topics to each customer&#39;s business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, brief, and coach executive and technical speakers, ensuring every session lands with clarity and a consistent narrative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end onsite execution: room and space experience, catering, branding, demos, technology, and hospitality details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a library of briefing content, discussion frameworks, and demo experiences in partnership with Product Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage program operations including budget, vendor relationships, capacity planning, and briefing calendars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and report on program metrics such as briefings delivered, pipeline influenced, deal acceleration, and attendee satisfaction, and use that data to improve the program each quarter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend the program over time to strategic formats such as roadshows, virtual briefings, and executive roundtables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in executive briefing programs, strategic events, executive engagement, or field marketing, ideally at an enterprise SaaS company or B2B technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have run high-stakes programs involving C-level customers and internal executives, and you are calm and precise under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional program management skills: you juggle many briefings at different stages without letting details slip&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and the ability to translate account strategy into a compelling briefing agenda&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicator who can brief a CEO, coach a speaker, and negotiate with a vendor in the same afternoon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with a technical audience and product; you can hold your own in conversations about developer platforms, cloud infrastructure, and AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-oriented: you measure what matters and can articulate program ROI to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in or willing to relocate to the San Francisco Bay Area, with flexibility for occasional travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus If You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built an EBC or briefing program from zero to scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with briefing management platforms and CRM reporting (Salesforce)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked closely with developer or infrastructure products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience designing physical brand spaces or customer experience centers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $150,000 - $207,000. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don&#39;t necessarily check every box on the job description.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-copy-16 text-gray-900 [&amp;amp;_b]:text-gray-1000 my-6 [&amp;amp;_b]:font-semibold [&amp;amp;_i]:not-italic&quot;&gt;#LI-KS1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;te-floating-button-container&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company. We free people and agents to ship what’s next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For more than a decade, Vercel has shaped how the web is built. As the team behind Next.js, v0, and AI SDK, we create products that help builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now, software is entering a new era, and the next generation of products will not just be used by people. They will be built, extended, and operated by agents.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We are building the platform for that future, trusted by companies like&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide&lt;/strong&gt;. Whether you’re building our products, supporting our customers, growing our community, or shaping our story, you’ll help define what comes next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Forward-Deployed Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;to join our Professional Services team. This role is focused on working directly alongside developer teams in our most strategic enterprise customers to drive transformational outcomes across frontend modernization, platform migrations, and AI adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead complex Next.js migrations, architect high-performance applications, and build production AI solutions - all within customer environments. You&#39;ll work hands-on-keyboard alongside customer teams, whether you&#39;re migrating a legacy React application to App Router, conducting a deep-dive code audit, or deploying production agents using Vercel&#39;s eve framework and AI SDK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Forward-Deployed Engineers operate with high agency and autonomy. You&#39;ll navigate ambiguous enterprise environments, assess technical debt, design migration strategies, and deliver measurable business value - all while building long-term relationships that expand our partnership with each customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are two main profiles for this role: Next.js experts, and AI builders. Next.js experts work on deep customer code optimization, performance audits, AEO and SEO, and teaching customers how to build Next.js apps with AI instrumentation - such as Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, etc with Next.js and Vercel agent skills. The AI builder profile is less focused on deep Next.js experience, and more on identifying, evangelizing, and building AI applications and agentic workflows. Your job in this role will be to understand customers’ businesses, scope, design, and build AI agents, and prove their value. The two profiles are not mutually exclusive and we appreciate expertise in both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Global Manager of Forward Deployed Engineering. This role is remote-first with travel to customer sites expected occasionally. Travel requirements vary, but most of our engineers travel no more than 3-4 days every other month.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build production AI solutions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;using Vercel&#39;s&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;eve&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;framework, AI SDK, and AI Cloud infrastructure, including conversational interfaces, production agents, MCP servers, and agentic workflows that transform customer operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead complex frontend migrations -&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;modernizing legacy React, Vue, or other frameworks to Next.js, including Pages to App Router transitions, incremental adoption strategies, and large-scale codebase transformations. Automation of migrations is key to engineering efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conduct code audits and help analyze and improve website performance&lt;/strong&gt;, analyzing customer codebases for performance bottlenecks, architectural anti-patterns, and optimization opportunities - delivering actionable roadmaps that drive measurable improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect and implement high-performance Next.js applications&lt;/strong&gt;, leveraging App Router, Server Components, streaming, ISR, and advanced rendering strategies to meet enterprise scale and performance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embed with strategic customers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;to build production applications - working within their systems, understanding their constraints, and shipping TypeScript code that goes live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive enablement and knowledge transfer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;through workshops, pair programming, and documentation - ensuring customer teams can extend and maintain solutions independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navigate complex enterprise environments&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;by building relationships with stakeholders across engineering, product, and executive teams - translating technical capabilities into business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to our service evolution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;by identifying repeatable patterns, building reusable components, and sharing implementation insights back to Product and Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6+ years of experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;in software engineering with at least 2 years in a customer-facing technical role (consulting, solutions architecture, forward deployed engineering, or technical founder experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience using AI instrumentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;such as harnesses, skills, and MCPs to build and deploy web applications, backend systems, and/or agentic workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
