&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company. We free people and agents to ship what’s next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For more than a decade, Vercel has shaped how the web is built. As the team behind Next.js, v0, and AI SDK, we create products that help builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now, software is entering a new era, and the next generation of products will not just be used by people. They will be built, extended, and operated by agents.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We are building the platform for that future, trusted by companies like&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide&lt;/strong&gt;. Whether you’re building our products, supporting our customers, growing our community, or shaping our story, you’ll help define what comes next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Next.js team builds the open source framework that powers millions of applications and shapes how developers build for the web. Our work sits at the intersection of React, framework architecture, developer experience, infrastructure, performance, and production reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Engineering Team Lead to help build and lead a team working on Next.js. This is a hands-on player/coach role for an experienced engineer who wants to remain close to the code while helping a small team do its best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be an engineer first and a manager second. You will contribute directly to the framework, lead major technical initiatives, review code, debug complex production issues, and help make architectural decisions. You will also support the engineers around you through clear direction, thoughtful feedback, and practical coaching.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional people management role. You will spend the majority of your time on technical leadership and engineering execution. You should be comfortable owning difficult parts of the codebase while creating enough context and clarity for others to move quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Product, Design, and engineers across Vercel to guide the evolution of Next.js across rendering, caching, routing, build systems, and developer tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and ship Next.js:&lt;/strong&gt; Write production code, review pull requests, debug difficult issues, and contribute directly to the framework and its supporting systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead major technical initiatives:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of complex projects from initial exploration through architecture, implementation, rollout, and production follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set technical direction:&lt;/strong&gt; Make sound architectural decisions across rendering, caching, routing, build systems, runtime behavior, and developer tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay close to real problems:&lt;/strong&gt; Investigate performance regressions, production failures, and developer pain points. Turn what you learn into practical improvements to the framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the engineering bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish strong patterns for code quality, testing, performance, reliability, observability, and incremental delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coach through the work:&lt;/strong&gt; Help engineers grow through pairing, design reviews, code reviews, technical feedback, and shared ownership of challenging problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide focused people leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Set clear expectations, give candid feedback, support career development, and help maintain a high-trust and accountable team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve team execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Create lightweight planning and decision-making practices that clarify ownership, reduce unnecessary coordination, and help the team ship consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across Vercel:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Product, Design, Infrastructure, Developer Experience, and other engineering teams so framework changes integrate cleanly across the Vercel platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion open source:&lt;/strong&gt; Work in public, engage thoughtfully with contributors, and balance community needs with the team’s product and technical priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help grow the team:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in recruiting, assess technical talent, and help new engineers become productive in a complex codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of software engineering experience and remain highly effective as a hands-on engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have led engineers or small technical teams, whether as a team lead, tech lead, staff engineer, engineering manager, or founder.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have recent experience writing, reviewing, and shipping production code. You are not looking to step away from engineering execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong technical judgment across React, framework architecture, or the systems behind a large-scale open source project, including rendering, caching, routing, build tooling, and runtime behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can take a complex technical problem, form a clear point of view, write the critical code, and bring other engineers along with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know when to lead from the front and when to create space for someone else to take ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building products or infrastructure for developers and understand the quality, performance, stability, and usability standards this audience expects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think in systems and can guide a team toward clean abstractions, consistent framework patterns, and technical decisions that hold up at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working through ambiguity and solving problems from first principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You balance speed and quality. You favor incremental delivery and real-world feedback while recognizing when foundational infrastructure requires deeper investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly in writing, facilitate productive technical debate, and make decisions when a path forward is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI tools in your own workflow and have informed opinions about how agentic products should work for developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining or contributing to a major open source project, particularly in the React or Next.js ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with compilers, bundlers, caching, rendering systems, or distributed infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a small, senior engineering team while continuing to make substantial individual contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience forming a team or technical direction from zero to one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Next.js codebase, though this is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive healthcare package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and growth support, including mentorship and opportunities to attend events that build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible time off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The equipment you need to do your role, plus a work-from-home budget to outfit your space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $230,000 to $340,000. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program, depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate based on race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel encourages everyone to apply, even if they do not meet every qualification listed in the job description.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company. We free people and agents to ship what’s next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For more than a decade, Vercel has shaped how the web is built. As the team behind Next.js, v0, and AI SDK, we create products that help builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now, software is entering a new era, and the next generation of products will not just be used by people. They will be built, extended, and operated by agents.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We are building the platform for that future, trusted by companies like&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide&lt;/strong&gt;. Whether you’re building our products, supporting our customers, growing our community, or shaping our story, you’ll help define what comes next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Manager of Solutions Architecture to join and lead our our Americas SA team. In this role, you will be responsible for leading a team of Solutions Architects who support our&amp;nbsp; sales teams across pre and post sales. You will drive technical excellence, mentor the team, and partner closely with sales leadership to win new business and expand existing accounts. This is a&amp;nbsp; hybrid role (3 days per week in office) based in our San Francisco, New York, or Austin office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and manage an AMER SA team, including training and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure technical excellence across the pre and post sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on support for key accounts as needed (presentations, architecture reviews, migration plans).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and coach SA engagement on strategic accounts and critical deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our engineering org to provide product feedback from the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop repeatable plays from trends your are seeing across your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report SA performance to Sales and Field Engineering leadership quarterly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own org planning, staffing, budgeting, and regional recruiting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in Solutions Architecture/Engineering, Sales Engineering, or Technical Pre-sales roles, with at least 2+ years in a leadership position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in web technologies (Next.js, React, Node.js, APIs, cloud infrastructure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead, coach, and scale technical teams in a high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success working with enterprise and commercial customers across diverse industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern software development workflows (CI/CD, DevOps, frontend frameworks).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with Sales, Product, and Engineering teams to drive customer success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus if you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working with Vercel, Next.js, or similar frontend frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have led SA teams at a high-growth SaaS or cloud infrastructure company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring expertise in developer tooling, edge computing, or performance optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable presenting at conferences, webinars, or large-scale customer events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The San Francisco, CA base OTE pay range for this role is $245,000.00 - $307,000.00. This OTE range is an estimate. Actual salary will be based on job related skills, experience and location. Pay ranges outside San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location.&amp;nbsp; The total compensation package also includes benefits and equity-based compensation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don&#39;t necessarily check every box on the job description.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company. We free people and agents to ship what’s next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For more than a decade, Vercel has shaped how the web is built. As the team behind Next.js, v0, and AI SDK, we create products that help builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now, software is entering a new era, and the next generation of products will not just be used by people. They will be built, extended, and operated by agents.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We are building the platform for that future, trusted by companies like&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide&lt;/strong&gt;. Whether you’re building our products, supporting our customers, growing our community, or shaping our story, you’ll help define what comes next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Marketing Operations Manager to join our Marketing Operations team within the broader Revenue Operations organization. This is a hands-on, technical generalist role for someone who loves owning the operational machinery behind a fast-moving GTM team—and who&#39;s excited to run it faster using modern AI-assisted tooling like v0, Claude Code, and the Vercel platform itself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own and evolve the systems, data, and workflows that power our marketing motions: administering and integrating our martech stack, keeping our data clean and trustworthy, and building the campaigns and lifecycle automations that drive pipeline. This isn&#39;t a pure admin seat and it isn&#39;t an engineering seat—it&#39;s for an operator who&#39;s comfortable getting under the hood, automating the manual stuff, and prototyping their own solutions instead of waiting on a backlog.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Senior Manager, Marketing Operations and can be located remote (US-based in the Pacific, Mountain, or Central time zone) or hybrid out of our San Francisco HQ or Austin office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer our core martech stack—including our marketing automation platform (&lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;) and its integration with Salesforce, Snowflake, and downstream systems —keeping tools tightly connected and data flowing reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, QA, and launch marketing campaigns and email programs in partnership with Growth Marketing, ensuring clean execution and measurable results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain lifecycle, nurture, and automation flows that move leads through the funnel and support segmentation and personalization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own data hygiene and governance across marketing systems—deduplication, normalization, enrichment, and the standards that keep our data trustworthy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-native dev tools (v0, Claude Code, Vercel) to build internal helpers, automate repetitive workflows, and prototype solutions to ops problems quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with RevOps and GTM Analytics to ensure reliable lead flow and reporting, proactively flagging gaps, bottlenecks, or tech debt before they become problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of Marketing Operations experience in SaaS or high-growth startups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on operator who not only administers the martech stack but actively improves and automates it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with marketing automation platforms (e.g. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;, Marketo) and CRM systems (e.g. Salesforce)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with integration and data-routing tools (e.g. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Tray.io&quot;&gt;Tray.io&lt;/a&gt;, RudderStack, Segment)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience with AI-native development tools like v0, Cursor, or similar—and genuinely excited to use them to move fast on early ideas&lt;/strong&gt; (this is core to how this team works)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable reading and lightly editing code, and writing basic SQL to pull and validate data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong instincts for data quality and detail, with a bias toward fixing root causes over patching symptoms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in ambiguity and a fast-moving environment, and likes owning problems end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus If You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience with TypeScript, more advanced SQL, or data modeling for GTM systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built or scaled systems in support of PLG motions or developer-focused products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built internal tools or ops automations that went beyond stitching existing platforms together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience building on Vercel or similar modern web platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $140,000 - $210,000. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
